; Ordinals must match the real system dxgi.dll exactly.
;
; The d3d12.dll proxy already learned this the expensive way: the Windows SDK's
; d3d12.lib imports D3D12CreateDevice BY ORDINAL, and a proxy with the right
; names but linker-assigned ordinals fails to load with STATUS_ORDINAL_NOT_FOUND
; (0xC0000138) before any of our code runs. Same discipline here, and dxgi has
; the added hazard that the ordinals are NOT in alphabetical order.
;
; Real table (Win11 26100, dumpbin /exports C:\Windows\System32\dxgi.dll):
;    1 ApplyCompatResolutionQuirking    11 CreateDXGIFactory1
;    2 CompatString                     12 CreateDXGIFactory2
;    3 CompatValue                      13 DXGID3D10CreateDevice
;    4 DXGIDumpJournal                  14 DXGID3D10CreateLayeredDevice
;    5 PIXBeginCapture                  15 DXGID3D10GetLayeredDeviceSize
;    6 PIXEndCapture                    16 DXGID3D10RegisterLayers
;    7 PIXGetCaptureState               17 DXGIDeclareAdapterRemovalSupport
;    8 SetAppCompatStringPointer        18 DXGIDisableVBlankVirtualization
;    9 UpdateHMDEmulationStatus         19 DXGIGetDebugInterface1
;   10 CreateDXGIFactory                20 DXGIReportAdapterConfiguration
;
; The three CreateDXGIFactory entry points are C forwarders in dxgi_proxy.cpp,
; because the adapter hook is installed from them. The other seventeen have no
; public signature and are tail-jump thunks in dxgi_thunks.asm, which need none.
;
; Every one of them matters. d3d11.dll, d3d12.dll, the display driver and PIX
; all import from "dxgi.dll" by name, and inside this process that name is US.
; A missing export is a load failure somewhere that has nothing to do with us.

LIBRARY dxgi
EXPORTS
    ApplyCompatResolutionQuirking     @1
    CompatString                      @2
    CompatValue                       @3
    DXGIDumpJournal                   @4
    PIXBeginCapture                   @5
    PIXEndCapture                     @6
    PIXGetCaptureState                @7
    SetAppCompatStringPointer         @8
    UpdateHMDEmulationStatus          @9
    CreateDXGIFactory                 @10
    CreateDXGIFactory1                @11
    CreateDXGIFactory2                @12
    DXGID3D10CreateDevice             @13
    DXGID3D10CreateLayeredDevice      @14
    DXGID3D10GetLayeredDeviceSize     @15
    DXGID3D10RegisterLayers           @16
    DXGIDeclareAdapterRemovalSupport  @17
    DXGIDisableVBlankVirtualization   @18
    DXGIGetDebugInterface1            @19
    DXGIReportAdapterConfiguration    @20
